    title: { zh: "超加工食品的机制科学与食物基质", en: "Mechanistic Science of Ultra-Processed Foods and the Food Matrix" },
    qfocus: { zh: "配平热量、糖、盐与纤维后仍多摄入的约 500 大卡，究竟来自基质结构、进食速度还是适口性？", en: "After calories, sugar, salt and fiber are matched, where do the roughly 500 extra kilocalories come from — matrix structure, eating rate, or hyperpalatability?" },
    domain: "生命",
    cluster: { code: "C24", zh: "未来食品·农业科学", en: "Future food · agricultural science" },
    scores: [4, 4, 3, 3, 5, 4, 4, 4, 4],
    citation: {
      url: "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cmet.2019.05.020",
      title: "Ultra-Processed Diets Cause Excess Calorie Intake and Weight Gain: An Inpatient Randomized Controlled Trial of Ad Libitum Food Intake",
      venue: "Cell Metabolism",
      year: 2019,
    },
    brief: { zh: "在代谢病房里把超加工的各个候选机制逐一拆开做随机对照——固定营养成分，只改变食物基质的物理结构、进食速度或能量密度——测量自由进食量、体重与代谢指标的因果贡献。", en: "Take the candidate mechanisms of ultra-processing apart one at a time in randomized metabolic-ward trials — holding nutrient composition fixed while varying only the physical structure of the food matrix, eating rate, or energy density — and measure the causal contribution to ad libitum intake, weight and metabolic markers." },
    literature: [
      { title: "Effect of Ultra-processed Versus Unprocessed Diets on Energy Metabolism (NCT05290064, completed Aug 2025)", venue: "NIH Clinical Center / ClinicalTrials.gov", year: 2025, url: "https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT05290064" },
      { title: "Eating rate has sustained effects on energy intake from ultraprocessed diets: a 2-week ad libitum RCT crossover trial", venue: "American Journal of Clinical Nutrition", year: 2025, url: "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ajcnut.2025.11.012" },
    ],
    depth: {
      overview: { zh: "Hall 团队 2019 年的代谢病房随机对照试验做了一件反直觉的事：把热量、能量密度、宏量营养素、糖、盐与纤维全部配平之后，受试者吃超加工餐每天仍多摄入约 508 大卡并增重。这把致病机制从营养成分表移到了食物基质的物理结构、口感与进食速度上。", en: "Hall's 2019 inpatient randomized controlled trial did something counterintuitive: with calories, energy density, macronutrients, sugar, salt and fiber all matched, participants on the ultra-processed diet still consumed about 508 more kilocalories per day and gained weight. That moves the causal mechanism off the nutrition-facts panel and onto the physical structure of the food matrix, its mouthfeel, and eating rate." },
      whyMatters: { zh: "如果多摄入不是由成分驱动，那么按营养素书写的膳食指南就在指错方向；但把「超加工有害」拆成可操作的机制变量至今没有做到，各机制彼此纠缠。", en: "If the excess intake is not driven by composition, dietary guidance written in nutrients is pointing the wrong way. Yet decomposing 'ultra-processed is harmful' into operable mechanistic variables has not been achieved — the candidate mechanisms remain entangled." },
      ifAnswered: { zh: "膳食建议可以从数营养素转向看结构与进食速度，食品配方也有了可监管、可测量的物理指标，而不只是分类标签。", en: "Dietary advice could shift from counting nutrients to reading structure and eating rate, and food formulation would gain measurable, regulatable physical indicators instead of a classification label." },
      approaches: [
        { zh: "在代谢病房里固定热量与宏量营养素，只改变基质完整度，测自由进食量的差异。", en: "In the metabolic ward, hold calories and macronutrients fixed and vary only matrix integrity, measuring the difference in ad libitum intake." },
        { zh: "用两周自由进食交叉试验单独操纵进食速度，检验它对能量摄入是否有持续效应。", en: "Manipulate eating rate alone in a two-week ad libitum crossover trial to test whether its effect on energy intake is sustained." },
        { zh: "在 NIH 已完成的多机制试验框架下，并行比较能量密度与超适口性两条通路。", en: "Within the framework of the completed NIH multi-mechanism trial, compare the energy-density and hyperpalatability pathways in parallel." },
      ],
      barrier: { zh: "基质崩解、进食速度、能量密度与超适口性在真实食物里天然共变，很难只动一个；而能做到严格配平的代谢病房试验样本小、成本高、时长有限。", en: "Matrix disintegration, eating rate, energy density and hyperpalatability co-vary naturally in real food, so moving just one is hard — and the metabolic-ward trials that can enforce strict matching are small, expensive and short." },
      subQuestions: [
        { zh: "口腔加工阶段的基质崩解速率，能否成为可测量、可写进配方规格的中间变量？", en: "Can the rate of matrix disintegration during oral processing become a measurable intermediate variable written into formulation specifications?" },
        { zh: "进食速度的效应是通过饱腹信号的延迟实现的，还是通过每一口的能量密度实现的？", en: "Does the eating-rate effect work through delayed satiety signaling, or through the energy density of each bite?" },
        { zh: "同一份超加工食品，仅通过改变物理结构而不动配方，能把多摄入压回多少？", en: "For the same ultra-processed food, how much of the excess intake can be recovered by changing physical structure alone, leaving the recipe untouched?" },
      ],
    },
