    scores: [4, 5, 5, 2, 3, 2, 5, 3, 4],
    citation: {
      url: "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41596-025-01145-9",
      title: "Spatially resolved genome-wide joint profiling of epigenome and transcriptome with spatial-ATAC-RNA-seq and spatial-CUT&Tag-RNA-seq",
      venue: "Nature Protocols",
      year: 2025,
    },
    brief: { zh: "沿用 Rong Fan 实验室的确定性微流控条码，在一张组织切片上同时捕获染色质可及性或组蛋白修饰与 mRNA，把 3–5 天的标准流程移植到新组织，并检验表观与转录状态的空间共变是否稳定。", en: "Adopt the Rong Fan lab's deterministic microfluidic barcoding to capture chromatin accessibility or histone marks together with mRNA on a single tissue section, port the 3–5 day standard protocol to new tissues, and test whether the spatial covariation of epigenetic and transcriptional state holds up." },
    literature: [
      { title: "Spatially resolved epigenome sequencing via Tn5 transposition and deterministic DNA barcoding in tissue", venue: "Nature Protocols", year: 2024, url: "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41596-024-01013-y" },
      { title: "Spatial epigenome–transcriptome co-profiling of mammalian tissues", venue: "Nature", year: 2023, url: "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-023-05795-1" },
    ],
    depth: {
      overview: { zh: "spatial-ATAC-RNA-seq 与 spatial-CUT&Tag-RNA-seq 用同一套确定性微流控条码，在切片上按行列交叉写入空间地址，使表观层与转录层共享同一坐标系。范式转移在于：因果链不再靠算法事后配准两个独立数据集，而是在原位被同时读出。", en: "spatial-ATAC-RNA-seq and spatial-CUT&Tag-RNA-seq write spatial addresses onto a section by crossed rows and columns of one deterministic microfluidic barcode set, so the epigenetic and transcriptional layers share a single coordinate frame. The paradigm move: the causal chain is no longer stitched together computationally from two independent datasets after the fact, but read out in situ at the same time." },
      whyMatters: { zh: "细胞身份由表观调控决定，可基因组级表观信号（尤其新鲜冷冻组织的 ATAC）本就信噪比偏低；要同时保住空间坐标与多层灵敏度，分辨率、覆盖度、通量难以同时拉满。", en: "Cell identity is set by epigenetic regulation, yet genome-wide epigenetic signal — ATAC on fresh-frozen tissue above all — is intrinsically low in signal-to-noise; holding spatial coordinates and multi-layer sensitivity at once means resolution, coverage and throughput cannot all be maximized together." },
      ifAnswered: { zh: "胚胎与成体脑组织里「表观状态如何决定细胞类型动态」可以直接在原位读出，而不再依赖跨数据集的计算对齐假设。", en: "How epigenetic state governs cell-type dynamics in embryonic and adult brain tissue could be read directly in situ, no longer resting on the assumptions behind cross-dataset computational alignment." },
      approaches: [
        { zh: "把 spatial-ATAC-seq 与 spatial-CUT&Tag 的 Tn5 转座与抗体化学接进同一条码流程，逐层核对像素级配准。", en: "Fold the Tn5 transposition of spatial-ATAC-seq and the antibody chemistry of spatial-CUT&Tag into one barcoding workflow, checking pixel-level registration layer by layer." },
        { zh: "按 Nature Protocols 2025 的 3–5 天流程与开源分析管线在新组织复跑，报告每层的有效像素与丢失率。", en: "Rerun the 3–5 day Nature Protocols 2025 workflow and its open-source analysis pipeline on new tissues, reporting usable pixels and dropout per layer." },
        { zh: "用同一切片的连续切面做正交验证：单细胞多组学、免疫组化与成像类空间转录组交叉核对。", en: "Validate orthogonally on serial sections of the same block: cross-check against single-cell multi-omics, immunohistochemistry and imaging-based spatial transcriptomics." },
      ],
      barrier: { zh: "表观层信号稀疏且随组织固定方式漂移；条码像素并非真正单细胞，一个像素里混着的细胞类型会把「表观→转录」的因果读成共变。", en: "The epigenetic layer is sparse and drifts with fixation chemistry, and a barcoded pixel is not truly one cell — the cell types mixed inside a pixel turn an 'epigenetics → transcription' causal claim back into mere covariation." },
      subQuestions: [
        { zh: "在同一像素内，染色质可及性的变化是否在时间上先于对应基因的 mRNA 变化，还是只在群体水平共变？", en: "Within one pixel, does a change in chromatin accessibility precede the mRNA change of the corresponding gene in time, or do the two only covary at the population level?" },
        { zh: "把组蛋白修饰换成 DNA 甲基化或三维构象层后，确定性条码的空间分辨率与灵敏度会各损失多少？", en: "If histone marks are swapped for DNA methylation or a 3D-conformation layer, how much spatial resolution and how much sensitivity does deterministic barcoding each give up?" },
        { zh: "新鲜冷冻与 FFPE 组织之间，同一区域的表观—转录耦合强度是否可重复，差异能否被归因到样本处理？", en: "Is the epigenome–transcriptome coupling strength of the same region reproducible between fresh-frozen and FFPE tissue, and can the difference be attributed to sample handling?" },
      ],
    },
